Relevant tables, columns and how they can help  

• PLANET_FEATURES  
  – "feature_type": limit the search to ‘multipolygons’.  
  – "all_tags": JSON array that can hold { "key":"wikidata", "value":"Q1095" }.  
  – "geometry": WKB geometry that can be converted to GEOGRAPHY and spatially compared with relations.  

• PLANET_RELATIONS  
  – "all_tags": check for a “name” key (must exist) and ensure no key “wikidata”.  
  – "geometry": WKB geometry; intersect / contain tests against the Q1095 multipolygon.  
  – "members": list of child objects – later flattened to see whether at least one child has a wikidata tag.  
  – "id": join key when checking its members in PLANET_FEATURES (by way / node / relation id).  

• Additional PLANET_FEATURES columns used later  
  – "osm_id", "osm_way_id": can be matched to integers in "members".  
  – "geometry": again, for “features contained in the relation” counts.  


Below are ten Snowflake SQL snippets, ordered from exploratory to near‑final.  
All identifiers are quoted; each query is capped with LIMIT 20 just to sample results.  
Convert the WKB to GEOGRAPHY with TO_GEOGRAPHY for spatial predicates.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Grab the multipolygon(s) that are tagged with wikidata = Q1095.
SELECT
  "osm_id",
  "osm_way_id",
  "feature_type",
  "all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES"
WHERE "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "all_tags") t
        WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
          AND t.value:"value"::STRING = 'Q1095'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Look at the geometry for the Q1095 multipolygon (sample only).
SELECT
  TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS "geom_q1095"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES"
WHERE "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "all_tags") t
        WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
          AND t.value:"value"::STRING = 'Q1095'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List relations that spatially intersect the Q1095 geometry and have a name tag.
WITH q AS (
  SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES"
  WHERE "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
    AND EXISTS (
          SELECT 1
          FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "all_tags") t
          WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
            AND t.value:"value"::STRING = 'Q1095'
        )
  LIMIT 1
)
SELECT
  r."id",
  r."all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r, q
WHERE ST_INTERSECTS(
        TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"),
        q.g )
  AND EXISTS (           -- has a name tag
        SELECT 1
        FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t
        WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'name'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Filter out relations that themselves already carry a wikidata tag.
SELECT
  r."id",
  r."all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r
WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'name')
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Combine 3 + 4 – relations intersecting Q1095, having a name, but no wikidata.
WITH q AS (
  SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES"
  WHERE "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
    AND EXISTS (
          SELECT 1
          FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "all_tags") t
          WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
            AND t.value:"value"::STRING = 'Q1095'
        )
  LIMIT 1
)
SELECT
  r."id",
  r."all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r, q
WHERE ST_INTERSECTS(TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q.g)
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'name')
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Preview the member ids of candidate relations (flatten "members").
SELECT
  r."id"          AS "relation_id",
  m.value::STRING AS "member_id"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
WHERE r."id" = <PUT_RELATION_ID_HERE>
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Among those member ids, find which ones have a wikidata tag in PLANET_FEATURES.
SELECT
  p."osm_id",
  p."all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES" p
WHERE p."osm_id" IN (SELECT m.value::NUMBER
                     FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r,
                          LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
                     WHERE r."id" = <PUT_RELATION_ID_HERE>)
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."all_tags") t
        WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Count how many planet_features lie inside each candidate relation’s geometry.
WITH q AS (
  SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES"
  WHERE "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
    AND EXISTS (
          SELECT 1
          FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "all_tags") t
          WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
            AND t.value:"value"::STRING = 'Q1095'
        )
  LIMIT 1
), cand AS (
  SELECT r."id", TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry") AS rg
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r, q
  WHERE ST_INTERSECTS(TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q.g)
    AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'name')
    AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata')
)
SELECT
  c."id"                        AS "relation_id",
  COUNT(*)                      AS "features_inside"
FROM cand c
JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES" f
  ON ST_INTERSECTS(TO_GEOGRAPHY(f."geometry"), c.rg)
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 2 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Keep only the relation(s) whose members include at least one wikidata‑tagged feature.
WITH member_wd AS (
  SELECT
    r."id" AS relation_id
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
  JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES" p
       ON p."osm_id" = m.value::NUMBER
  WHERE EXISTS (
          SELECT 1
          FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."all_tags") t
          WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
        )
)
SELECT DISTINCT relation_id
FROM member_wd
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – name of the relation that intersects Q1095, has no wikidata,
--     contains the largest number of features, and includes at least one wikidata‑tagged member.
WITH q AS (
  SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES"
  WHERE "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
    AND EXISTS (
          SELECT 1
          FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "all_tags") t
          WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
            AND t.value:"value"::STRING = 'Q1095'
        )
  LIMIT 1
), candidate_relations AS (
  SELECT
    r."id",
    r."all_tags",
    TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry") AS rg
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r, q
  WHERE ST_INTERSECTS(TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q.g)
    AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'name')
    AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata')
), with_member_wd AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT cr."id", cr."all_tags", cr.rg
  FROM candidate_relations cr
  JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r2
    ON r2."id" = cr."id"
  , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r2."members") m
  JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES" p
    ON p."osm_id" = m.value::NUMBER
  WHERE EXISTS (
          SELECT 1
          FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."all_tags") t
          WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'wikidata'
        )
), counts AS (
  SELECT
    wmw."id",
    (SELECT t.value:"value"::STRING
       FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => wmw."all_tags") t
       WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'name'
       LIMIT 1)                       AS relation_name,
    COUNT(*)                          AS features_inside
  FROM with_member_wd wmw
  JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES" f
    ON ST_INTERSECTS(TO_GEOGRAPHY(f."geometry"), wmw.rg)
  GROUP BY 1,2
)
SELECT relation_name
FROM counts
ORDER BY features_inside DESC
LIMIT 20;
```


These queries walk through locating the Q1095 multipolygon, narrowing to the candidate relations, verifying their tag constraints, ensuring at least one wikidata‑tagged member, counting contained features, and finally selecting the relation name with the highest feature count.
